REALLY?!?!  Wow!  Its about time!!!

A bit of background....I was the sysop of a sequence of BBS systems in the
Minneapolis-St. Paul area over the last 12 years or so.  I knew this John
Michael Polzer very*** well.  Every six months or so, he would start
harassing all the local sysops by attempting to scroll message bases (by
posting garbage), harassing users through mail, and all the usual immature
things that 12-year-olds do the first time they encounter a BBS.  What made
this guy unique was that he persisted over a decade in his immaturity (most
kids are satisfied by just doing it once).  Several of the local sysops tried
repeatedly to take some sort of legal action against him (such as prosecution
under the Minnesota Computer Crime Statute, which makes computer vandalism
illegal), only to encounter indifferent (at best) or even hostile reactions
from the local law enforcement agencies.

Eventually, we pretty much gave up trying to have him arrested, and put
security in our BBS software that would allow us to counter his usual methods
of vandalism (generally with some effort).

At any rate, I'm glad to hear that someone has finally convinced the local
cops to do something about this guy.  I hope the judge takes away his modem
for good.

-Peter

