The Minnesota case might be different, but about two years ago, an incident
that would fit the original description given by Carl happened in Germany.

In this case the accused was alleged to have inflicted bodily harm and to
have harrassed and insulted another person via IRC. The case went to court
but was dropped (about one year after the incident).

Unfortunately, this means that no clear verdict was given by the judge. As
criminal cases in Germany are strictly oral, this also means that there is
no (official) written record of the hearing (or the lawsuit).

On the other hand, there was no serious analysis or attempt at definition
on part of the judge of how traditional jurisdictional terms apply to the
world of electronic media, e.g. what evidence should be considered, what
bodily harm and libel mean, in how far privacy protection laws apply (to
ensure validity of some kinds of illegally acquired evidence) etc.
